<Base title="About & Methodology — Federal Bench Reference">
  <div class="judgehead"><h1>About and methodology</h1></div>
  <section class="block">
    <h2>Sources</h2>
    <p class="summary">Biographical information for Article III judges is drawn from the Federal Judicial Center
    Biographical Directory. Magistrate-judge biographies are drawn from the court's own site. Opinions are linked
    to a free public copy — GovInfo or the issuing court first, then CourtListener or Justia.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="block">
    <h2>Verification standard</h2>
    <p class="summary">Every summary is written from the public opinion. Every link is verified to resolve to the
    correct case. Nothing about a sitting judge is published without human review. Where a link resolves only to an
    appellate opinion, the entry says so and does not attribute the appellate decision to the district judge.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="block">
    <h2>Limitations</h2>
    <p class="summary">This reference does not claim completeness for sealed matters, unpublished minute entries,
    oral decisions, subscription databases, or PACER-only documents. A statement that no publication was located
    records a search result as of a date, not an enduring negative fact. Magistrate-judge work is structurally
    underrepresented in free repositories.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="block">
    <h2>Independence</h2>
    <p class="summary">This reference is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or authorized by the United States
    courts or any judge. It describes what judges have decided. It does not predict what any judge will decide,
    and it publishes no per-judge statistics.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
